(I've submitted this to the development team.)

synopsis:

When you polymorph a non-boulder into a boulder, you can see
through/around the boulder.

steps to reproduce:

1) Go to a small room with no open/unlocked doors.
2) Wish for a large statue. (I used a mumak.)
3) Polymorph the statue into a boulder. You may have to redo
   steps 2 and 3 a few times until you get a boulder.
4) Wish for a peaceful creature that moves.
5) When the creature moves behind the boulder, you can still
   see the creature.
6) Leave the level, then return to the level.
7) The boulder now properly obscures what's behind it.

suggested fix:

Check for a non-boulder being turned into a boulder, and
ensure that you can't see through that newly formed boulder.

